    "rationale": "AF-CTR-03 part A2, hotfix 1 of Cloud #121, after af-ctr-03-r11 (which admitted fix round 2 at cloud-release-r72). Nothing new is admitted and nothing is corrected: the pages add no module (they use the standard library and the modules already locked: the published Contracts Go bindings, pgx, protobuf and the project's own packages), the twenty-two locked Go runtime modules and their legal records stay as admitted, and the isolated npm package eng/verification/browser (playwright-core 1.63.0, Apache-2.0, no further package or install script) is unchanged: its package.json, package-lock.json and .npmrc are the ones r9 admitted. center/go.mod, center/go.sum, center/dependencies.json, the root package-lock.json, the NuGet locks, the Dockerfile, the base images, the toolchains, .github/workflows/ci.yml and the root package.json are unchanged. The release profile cloud-release-r73 with its successor records center-runtime-r19 and center-worker-r19 binds the center sources (the Cache-Control value of the page routes) and the Worker sources (the redirect mode of every request to the Container, and the generated center tables with that value) as they are at this hotfix. The secret scan's generic-api-key rule reads the digests of go-gowebauthn-legal-r1 and go-gowebauthnx-legal-r1 in this receipt's inputs map as credentials, so .gitleaks.toml allows exactly those two rows of this receipt in a thirteenth exact-row block, pinned by tests/worker/provenance.test.ts. No D1 or business data migration and no new PostgreSQL migration: migration 0002's checksum is unchanged.",
